WEBVTT

﻿1

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.470
This is so good.


00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.730
I want more.


00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.520
Don't get greedy.


00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:30.980
Jeff?


00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.110
Hayley.


00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.190
Sorry.


00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.240
I was gonna be, like,
so sophisticated when we met.


00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.570
Little hard to do that with your mouth
full of...whatever that is.


00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.120
It's great. It's great.
Do you want some?


00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.410
Sure.


00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.330
Yum.


00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.250
It's, um... kind of
what I was thinking.


00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.380
Sorry?


00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:01.180
You just don't look like the kind of guy
who has to meet girls over the internet.


00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.600
I think it's better to meet people
online first sometimes.


00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.770
You get to know
what they're like inside.


00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.480
When you work as a photographer
you find out real quick, people's faces lie.


00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.280
Does my face lie?


00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.030
I look at those eyes
and I see...


00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.450
a girl who reads Zadie Smith,


00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.200
who listens to John Mayer
and ColdPlay,


00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:28.040
who loves Monty Python episodes


00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.910
and who, desperately,


00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.130
madly, deeply, wants,


00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.670
needs, longs for...
more chocolate.


00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.430
Excellent, excellent
judge of character.


00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.770
Can I get two of those truffles


00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.900
and two ganaches.


00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.020
Now what's a ganache?


00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.360
You don't know
what a ganache is?


00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.570
Lucky, you're with
a woman of the world


00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.240
to introduce you to these things.


00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.370
And two chocolate-covered hearts.


00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.120
And a decaf latte for me.


00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.200
- And...?
- I'm good.


00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.410
Yeah, you do appear so.


00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.210
So what's in the bag?


00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.250
Oh, you know,


00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.880
just, like, books and stuff.


00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:23.090
I figured if you stood me up,
then I should have something to read.


00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.100
Well... I couldn't really decide.


00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.390
I'm reading this book
about Jean Seberg.


00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:34.230
She's this actress
who slept with all the wrong people


00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.900
and ended up killing herself.


00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.360
Don't you do that.


00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.570
No. I intend to sleep
with all the right people.


00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.370
Plus, I'm reading Romeo and Juliet.


00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.870
It's a ninth grade book,


00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.500
but I figured I could have it done
before the school year starts, so...


00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.330
Doesn't look like
Elizabethan tragedy.


00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.380
No, that's 'cause--


00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.800
Well, my dad-- he's letting me audit
one of his med school courses, right?


00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.760
I don't really understand
half of it,


00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.590
but I totally love it.


00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.180
What?


00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.010
So you go to UCW


00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:12.430
and you sit in a lecture hall
with all these grad students


00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.560
and, what,
do they hit on you?


00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.610
Why? Are you jealous?


00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.780
Just admiring. I didn't know
you were interested in that kind of thing.


00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.860
What?


00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:27.490
You thought since we'd been chatting
for three weeks


00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.620
that you knew everything about me?


00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:35.290
Plus, they wouldn't hit on a 14-year-old girl.
They're old enough to be my dad, so...


00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.340
They're like...


00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.340
They're bad older.
They're-- You're not--


00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.510
I'm so articulate.


00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.340
Sorry. Can I just, like,
start over?


00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:50.810
No. I get it. I get it.
I just thought...


00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.060
You know, well,
you look older than you are.


00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.690
You certainly act
older than you are.


00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:00.690
Really?


00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.610
Yeah. I was expecting someone
not as impressive.


00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.910
Me too.


00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:14.870
Cool shirt.


00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.160
You want it?


00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.670
No, I didn't really bring
enough bucks, so...


00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.800
And yet, not actually
what I was asking.


00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.210
Sure, I want it.


00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.420
Can I get a green shirt
in a small, please?


00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.970
No. No, no.


00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.100
- I can't let you do that.
- What? Because--


00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.720
- Because--
- What? Because you'd be so


00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.560
indebted to me
that you'd have to...


00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.890
Okay. I guess I can
let you do that.


00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.730
You have to model it for me.


00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.070
Conditions. I can't live
with all these conditions.


00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.570
Thanks.


00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.950
- This is so unfair.
- What?


00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.620
This is when things happen,


00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.200
in the middle of the night, by which time
I am completely out of the scene.


00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.250
Life as a teenager.


00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.750
I just hate having to depend
Lindsey to drive me everywhere.


00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.340
You'll be driving
before you know it.


00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:06.590
In the meantime, I missed
Elizabeth Wurtzel speaking at USC


00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.220
and the Goldfrapp concert.


00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.140
I was at the Goldfrapp concert actually.


00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.600
Shut up. You were?
Was it great?


00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.520
Of course it was great.
What am I saying?


00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.640
Well, you could judge for yourself.


00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.100
- I got a bootleg MP3.
- You have the concert?


00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.690
Just one song. A little louder, please,
so the authorities know.


00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.240
I totally have to hear it.


00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.490
I'll send it to you.


00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.910
After you get home,
after you get around to it.


00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.910
Good things are worth the wait.


00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.620
And what have you waited for recently?


00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:41.080
I'm gonna have to wait
four years for you.


00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.540
You are just trying to distract me
from that MP3.


00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:46.170
Look, I have to send it.


00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.670
It's not like I could
take you to my house.


00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.340
That would be a little insane.


00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.680
True.


00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.260
Okay, now don't peek.


00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.220
I shoot models for a living.


00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.980
I've seen it all before.


00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.940
And you're so sure about that?


00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.230
I'm thinkin' yeah.


00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.610
Maybe you should peek


00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.570
and make that clerk wonder
what's going on over here.


00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.570
In your dreams, little girl.


00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.410
Little girl?


00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.660
Whatever happened to
how mature I was?


00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:20.870
- Is this mature enough for you?
- Okay...


00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:25.130
Keep teasing me like that,
you're gonna drive me crazy.


00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.000
Is that so?


00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.880
Okay. All right.


00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.300
How's this?


00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:34.970
Nice.


00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.350
Okay.


00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.430
Now, there's three points
I have to make.


00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:44.310
One: you wouldn't take advantage
because you've been seen with me.


00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:47.190
And two: it's Goldfrapp.


00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.480
And three?


00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.820
Well, and three--


00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:56.370
You said that it would be
insane for me to come over and...


00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:01.200
Four-- Four out of five doctors agree
that I am actually insane.


00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.210
Thus, I have to come over


00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.500
in order to be true to myself.


00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.840
Right?


00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.690
And the fourth reason:
this amazing car.


00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.110
Well, in the face of logic like that,
I bow down and worship.


00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.360
Bow down?


00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.360
That's a good idea.
What are you waiting for?


00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:37.660
Worship me.


00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.790
Yes, oh, royal Thonggirl.


00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.460
I am not worthy
to kiss your feet.


00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:50.050
Maybe you are.


00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.470
Maybe we should, like,
get going.


00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.310
Yes, oh, magnificent thonggirl.


00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:08.810
You wanna call your sister?
Tell her where you'll be?


00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.360
Maybe later.
I just wanna get in this car.


00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.960
Wow. So hot.


00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.430
What's wrong?


00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.680
Well, they teach us "young things"


00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.180
not to drink anything
we haven't mixed ourselves, so...


00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.850
Smart.


00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.360
Come back in the kitchen.
I'll pour it again.


00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.650
No. Come on.


00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.900
I can whip up something
more entertaining than that.


00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.370
Healthy dude, huh?


00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.000
I try.


00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.880
Figure I'll live
as long as I can.


00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.010
Living long is overrated.


00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.670
What? You don't want
to reach a ripe, old age?


00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.640
For what?
When I'm 80,


00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.720
what do I do for fun?


00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:08.180
When you're 80 I'll be 98.


00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:11.190
Right... and useless to me.


00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.020
What use do you have
in mind for me?


00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.910
I knew there'd be something
fun around here.


00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.710
I mean, other than wa--


00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.550
I bet these babes
got some dirt on you.


00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:39.710
Those are models.


00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:44.510
So why are they on your walls
instead of magazine covers?


00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.220
Here, looking at you while


00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:54.150
you know, you do the most
intimate things.


00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.020
My house is my studio.


00:13:56.110 --> 00:14:00.070
When clients come here they're walking
into my giant portfolio.


00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.320
So, what?
These were all shot here?


00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.080
Oh, my God.


00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.830
Okay, you are like
a big deal, aren't you?


00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.290
I get work.


00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.550
Isn't that one of those cameras
that gives you the square image?


00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.340
How do you know that?


00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:25.220
I'm a goon.
I just, like, read constantly.


00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.220
You saw all those books in my bag.


00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.100
You're not reading now.


00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.060
I'm not, am I?


00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.900
Feels good.


00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.070
Don't fall behind.


00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.780
We should toast.


00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.280
Carpe...


00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.370
omnious.


00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.160
What's that?


00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.710
It's my own little toast.


00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.290
You know carpe diem.


00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.590
"Seize the day."


00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.460
So I figure, carpe omnious.


00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.130
"Take it all."


00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.180
Take it all.


00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:17.400
So, like, what is it like
to look through your lens at some...


00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:20.150
beautiful woman
who's working so hard


00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.610
to look good for you?


00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:24.570
You know these models.
They all have handlers.


00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.240
People to make sure
their hair is just right


00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.740
and their makeup is okay


00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.870
and they don't get lost
on their way to their next gig.


00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.370
So you never get
to be alone with them?


00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.040
- Rarely.
- Poor Jeff.


00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.540
I am compensated for my troubles.
Don't worry about me.


00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:41.750
But I like worrying about you.


00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:47.010
It makes me wonder...


00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.180
What?


00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.140
No, no. Forget it.


00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:53.770
No, come on.


00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.640
Come on. What's in that
insane mind of yours?


00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:07.450
Okay. We'll have another screwdriver
and then maybe I'll tell you.


00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.450
- I'm waiting.
- Hold on.


00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.160
You are not keeping up.


00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.130
What?


00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.630
Okay, here's where you're supposed
to make it easier for me and read my mind.


00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.390
You're wondering how many
models I've done it with.


00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.350
No.


00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.560
- How many?
- None of them.


00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.730
- Oh, get out.
- No. They're underage, mostly.


00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.110
I'd be arrested.


00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.990
So you're not arrested
for photographing them like this?


00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.450
I'm very aware
of the legal boundaries.


00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.530
- I have to be.
- Right. Right.


00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.870
'Cause secretly...
Secretly...


00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.040
you would like to do them.


00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.580
No. There's just one
that I slept with


00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:03.750
when we were both younger.


00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.300
That one?


00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.420
No out here.


00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:11.470
- In the bedroom?
- No--


00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:21.020
What's her name?


00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.100
Hey.


00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.110
"Janelle."


00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.690
Yeah. Janelle.


00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:32.360
So, what? What? Was she, like,
the first big girlfriend or something?


00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.910
That's right.


00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.370
Learned everything I knew
practicing on her.


00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.160
And that date--


00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.670
Was that the first time
that you guys...


00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.710
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.


00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.880
So, what? Where is she now?


00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:54.340
She actually signed with Ford
right after this shoot.


00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.770
- She really took off. She, um...
- Oh, my God.


00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:02.940
She is, like, on magazine covers.
I know her.


00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.900
Well, like, not personally, obviously.


00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.690
You are impressive
every second.


00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.990
The models are impressive.
I just know how to bring it out.


00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.780
You still love her.


00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:16.990
No.


00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:18.410
Ah... yeah.


00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.490
- No.
- Yeah!


00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.700
- No.
- Really?


00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:22.210
- No.
- Really, really, really?


00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.250
No.


00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.090
I still love how simple things were
back then but...


00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.550
You know, I--


00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.510
I don't want to forget that, but...


00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.050
we've moved on.


00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.940
You're lonely.


00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.690
No.


00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.230
I can hear it in your voice.


00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:50.780
I'm a big boy.


00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:57.450
I guess everyone kind of
has a Janelle, right?


00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.030
I guess.


00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.950
Hey.


00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:03.790
What if you got
one of your cameras


00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.750
and we can see
what you can bring out in me.


00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:09.090
- This is what you wanted to ask?
- Well, I--


00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.590
- It's not as easy as you think.
- Okay.


00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.880
Models don't just pout their lips.


00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:16.340
They have to be willing
to open up.


00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:19.050
They have to show us
a little of their soul,


00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:21.310
their secrets.


00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.680
And most people only open up
from weakness.


00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:27.190
Nobody wants to see photos
of weak people.


00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.020
We look at great models
because they open up...


00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.030
from a position of...


00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:34.400
of, uh, of strength.


00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:36.450
They have the strength...


00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:38.110
to believe they can do anything,


00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:41.830
no matter how crazy, or, uh...


00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.450
Are you okay?


00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.290
- Let's try something.
- Okay.


